{title: Praise, My Soul, the King of Heaven}
{artist: Henry Lyte & John Goss}
{key: D}
{time: 2/4}
{tempo: 92}

Verse 1
[D]Praise, my soul, the [G]King of [D]heaven, [G]to his feet thy [A]tribute bring;
[D]ransomed, healed, re[G]stored, for[D]given, [Em]evermore his [A]praises [D]sing.
[A]Alleluia! [D]Alleluia! [G]Praise the ever[A]lasting [D]King.

Verse 2
[D]Praise Him for His grace [G]and favor [D]To our [G]fathers in distress. Praise Him [A]still the
[D]same as ever, Slow [Em]to chide, and [A]swift [D]to
[A]bless. [D]Alleluia! [G]Alleluia! Glorious in His [D]faithfulness.

Verse 3
[D]Father like He tends and [G]spares us; [D]Well our [G]feeble frame He knows. In [A]His hands
[D]He gently bears us, Rescues [Em]us from all [A]our [D]foes.
[A]Alleluia! [D]Alleluia! [G]Widely yet His mercy [D]flows.

Verse 4
[D]Frail as summer's flower we [G]flourish, Blows [D]the wind [G]and it is gone; But [A]while mortals
[D]rise and perish Our God [Em]lives unchanging on, [A]Praise [D]Him,
[A]Praise [D]Him, Hallelujah [G]Praise the High Eternal [D]One!

Verse 5
[D]Angels, help us to adore [G]Him; Ye [D]behold Him [G]face to face; Sun and [A]moon, bow
[D]down before Him, Dwellers all [Em]in time and [A]space. [D]Alleluia!
[A]Alleluia! [D]Praise with [G]us the God of [D]grace.
